  "description": "Stocks are dropping 17–22% overnight. I’m avoiding the wreckage and focusing on the assets offering better risk/reward.",
  "body_html": "<p>I keep getting asked: “Why silver?”, or more specifically, “Why Silver Miners?”</p><p>Because we care about % change… we want to have the highest % potential. </p><p>Here is an example. </p><p>Measuring from 2022:</p><ul><li><p>Gold bottomed in 2022, and peaked (locally) in March 2026 for <em><strong>220%. </strong></em></p></li><li><p>Silver in the same duration, ran approximately <strong>~375%</strong></p></li><li><p>The Top 4 Silver Mining Stocks: <em><strong>442%, 670%, 882% &amp; 1,248%</strong></em></p></li></ul><p>If gold goes up, then likely so will silver, then likely so will silver miners. </p><h4><strong>Lets make the most money we possibly can. These stocks have already started to reverse upwards. </strong></h4><p>If you are looking to get into Silver yourself, <em><strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/the-market-pulled-back-im-buying\">I have entry target posted here.</a></strong></em></p><p>Happy Friday to everyone! Pretty quiet day in the markets overall. S&amp;P 500 mostly just consolidated. Russel 2000 showed a bit more strength, but it was much of the same. </p><p>My market stance remains the same: consolidation into index funds and commodities like Silver. If you are new to my page, normally, we look for high momentum stocks to mid-term or long-term trade. We have slowed that approach, simply because too many stocks are “blowing up.” Looking at some the most talked about stocks today, that appears to be a good decision. </p><p>Lululemon and UiPath both crashed down -17%. Guidewire Software, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$GWRE&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> had a splendid earnings call, surpassing analysts estimates, and nearly doubling their EPS. What happened? Stock crashed -22%. </p><p>To be clear…no, Silver or Silver miners are <strong>NOT</strong> safe in a bear market. But they do normally give us more time, more runway. </p><p>This is why we are no stock picking. Too many stock landmines. We will focus on assets trending well, particularly “recession resistant” assets, which has been working fairly well for us. </p><p>Make sure you take some time off this weekend. Its so important to step away from the charts and headline noise. You come in far sharper Monday when you give yourself a break. </p><p>If you have questions, feel free to tag me in the <strong><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/d18286d6-5152-4f20-85c8-cedb68ee0e71\">Main Chat</a> </strong>during market hours. Have a great weekend, and I will see you Monday!</p><h4>Please like ❤️ and re-stack this post! It helps get out ahead of the AI slop here on Substack. </h4><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/too-many-stock-landmines-heres-where?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Know someone into investing? Share this post with them!</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/too-many-stock-landmines-heres-where?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/too-many-stock-landmines-heres-where?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><p></p>",
